<title>USA: Washington Savings to take one-time charge.</title>
<headline>Washington Savings to take one-time charge.</headline>
<dateline>WALDORF, Md. 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Washington Savings Bank said Tuesday that its first quarter earnings in 1997 will be reduced by a one-time, after-tax charge of about $1.04 million, or $0.23 per share for a special assessment.</p>
<p>The special assessment, which is related to recently enacted legislation, is to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>It was assessed at 65.7 basis points on assessable thrift deposits as of March 31, 1995, the company said.</p>
</text>
